JavaScript Interpretation:
    - When javascript runs it goes from two phases:
        1. Compilation Pahse (Hoisting)
        2. Execution Phase

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hoisting in Javascipt:
    - It is concept where "Function" or "varibale" are moved to the top of their scope.
    - It happens during "complition phase" before execution.

1. Hoisting of Varibale (var):

        console.log(name);  // undefined
        var name = "Shubh";

    - Javascipt will treat (interpret) above code as an:

        var name;
        console.log(name); // undefined
        name = "Shubh";

        --- as the name is not assign any value so we are getting undefined as a result.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Hoisting of Variable (let):

        console.log(name); // Reference Error
        let name = "Shubh";

    - Javascript will treat above code as an:

    A] Compilation Phase (Hoisting)
        store "let name" in Temporal Dead Zone (TDZ)
    
    B] Execution Phase :
        console.log(name); // Reference Error -> name is in Temporal Dead Zone
        let name = "Shubh"; // we got the initialization of "name" -> Temporal Dead Zone Ends here
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Hoisting of Function:

        Shubhzz();                     // Hello World
        function Shubhzz(){
            console.log("Hello World");
        }

    - Javascipt will treat above function code as an:
        A] Compilation phase:
            all the functions are stored in Hoisting.
        B] Execution Phase:
            Shubhzz(); // Function is called which stored in hoisting.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Hoisting of Var-Function:

        Shubhzz();                           // TypeError -> 'Shubhzz' is not a function
        var Shubhzz = function (){
            console.log("This is an Var function");
        }

    - Javascipt will treat above function code as an:
        A] Compilation phase:
            - 'Shubhzz' is declared as an Varibale 'var';
            - declare and store it in hoisting as an 'undefined' value

        B] Execution Phase:
            - Javascipt code will see it as an undefined so it will give output as it is not an function.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporal Dead Zone:
    - In Hoisting of Compilation phase all the Varibales and functions are goes on top of their scope.
    - When it 'var' variable gets on top of the scop as it is global scop varibale that why is has been declared but not assigned any value.
        var name;
    - When it 'let' or 'const' variable are moved to the top of their scope but not been declared and remained in Temporal Dead Zone.
        let name; <- not active present in Temporal Dead Zone.